
pip install paho-mqtt


Step 7: Configure Mosquitto (local offline broker)
Once Mosquitto is installed on Windows:
1. Open Command Prompt.
2. Navigate to the Mosquitto installation directory.
cd "C:\Program Files\mosquitto"


3. Start the local broker:
.\mosquitto.exe -v -p 1883


Keep this terminal open. If port 1883 is already in use because Mosquitto is running as a Windows service, use that existing broker instead of starting a second instance.
Step 8: Change both Python files for offline MQTT
In both publisher.py and subscriber.py, change:
broker = "broker.hivemq.com"



to:
broker = "localhost"



No other code changes are required.
Step 9: Run using Mosquitto (offline)
You can disconnect your internet connection because the broker is running locally.

Keep the Mosquitto broker running, then open two VS Code terminals.

Terminal 1 – Subscriber
python subscriber.py


Terminal 2 – Publisher
python publisher.py


Expected output:
Waiting for messages...
Temperature: 28.75 C
Humidity: 60.32 %
-----------------------
Temperature: 31.20 C
Humidity: 67.45 %
-----------------------


The local broker handles MQTT communication without an internet connection.